            <ArticleTitle>Status asthmaticus: is respiratory physiotherapy necessary?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>290-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a four year-old girl diagnosed of moderate extrinsic asthma that in the course of an episode of asthmatic status, she presented after treatment with respiratory physiotherapy an abrupt worsening of its clinical state, with appearance of a pneumotorax that precised intensive care treatment. The use of respiratory physiotherapy is dissuaded as part of the treatment in the initial phase of acute asthma, being reserved this treatment later in the recovery phase, anytime when a component of hypersecretion exists and the intensity of the bonchoconstriction has diminished.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
